s: 2004, 2005, 2006, 2007, 2008, 2009, 2010.\",\"temporalCoverage\":\"2004/2010\",\"spatialCoverage\":\"Gwinnett County Public Schools, Georgia, United States\",\"variableMeasured\":\"District graduation rate (%)\",\"citation\":[\"https://ted.cviog.uga.edu/financial-documents/sites/default/files/budgetdoc/financial-report/school-district-gwinnett-county-school-district-gwinnett-county-fy2013-financial-report.pdf\"],\"isBasedOn\":[\"https://ted.cviog.uga.edu/financial-documents/sites/default/files/budgetdoc/financial-report/school-district-gwinnett-county-school-district-gwinnett-county-fy2013-financial-report.pdf\"],\"isPartOf\":{\"@id\":\"#article\"}},{\"@type\":\"Dataset\",\"@id\":\"#data-four-year-graduation\",\"name\":\"Four-year graduation under the cohort calculation\",\"description\":\"Four-year graduation under the cohort calculation. District graduation rate (%). Reported years: 2016, 2017, 2018, 2019, 2020, 2021, 2022, 2023, 2024, 2025, 2026.\",\"temporalCoverage\":\"2016/2026\",\"spatialCoverage\":\"Gwinnett County Public Schools, Georgia, United States\",\"variableMeasured\":\"District graduation rate (%)\",\"citation\":[\"https://www.gcpsk12.org/news-details/~board/news-releases/post/gcps-graduation-rate-reaches-highest-point-in-a-decade-for-second-year-in-a-row\",\"https://www.gcpsk12.org/get-connected/district-news-and-communication/all-news/gcps-full-news-article/~board/news-releases/post/graduation-rates-are-on-the-rise-across-gcps\"],\"isBasedOn\":[\"https://www.gcpsk12.org/news-details/~board/news-releases/post/gcps-graduation-rate-reaches-highest-point-in-a-decade-for-second-year-in-a-row\",\"https://www.gcpsk12.org/get-connected/district-news-and-communication/all-news/gcps-full-news-article/~board/news-releases/post/graduation-rates-are-on-the-rise-across-gcps\"],\"isPartOf\":{\"@id\":\"#article\"}},{\"@type\":\"FAQPage\",\"@id\":\"#faq\",\"mainEntity\":[{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Which Gwinnett high schools made the biggest gains as a group?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Among neighborhood high schools with graduation results in both 2016 and 2025, the five with the lowest 2016 rates rose from an average of 71.0% to 84.5%. The five highest starters rose from 93.2% to 93.7%.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Did the highest-performing schools carry Gwinnett’s graduation rate?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"The higher-starting schools sustained high graduation rates. The lower-starting group improved faster. Calculating each group’s contribution to the districtwide gain requires its adjusted cohort sizes as well as its graduation rates.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Did reading improve in the same Gwinnett clusters?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"The district-level reading estimates used here cover grades 3–8. They cannot establish which feeder schools drove the decline or whether those schools belong to the same clusters that gained in graduation.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Does the data show higher-income families moving north within Gwinnett?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"The four maps show where income and child poverty changed. Establishing that families moved from southwest Gwinnett to northern Gwinnett also requires evidence of their origins and destinations.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Does this include Buford City Schools?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"The school results cover Gwinnett County Public Schools. Buford City Schools is a separate district. The county census maps cover a broader population than the GCPS student body.\"}}]},{\"@type\":\"Dataset\",\"@id\":\"#data-graduation-gap\",\"name\":\"Gwinnett high school graduation rates by 2016 starting group\",\"description\":\"Annual unweighted means for two fixed groups of five neighborhood high schools with official district graduation rates.\",\"temporalCoverage\":\"2016/2025\",\"variableMeasured\":\"Four-year graduation rate (%)\",\"isBasedOn\":\"https://www.gcpsk12.org/news-details/~board/news-releases/post/gcps-graduation-rate-reaches-highest-point-in-a-decade-for-second-year-in-a-row\",\"isPartOf\":{\"@id\":\"#article\"}},{\"@type\":\"Dataset\",\"@id\":\"#household-map\",\"name\":\"Gwinnett census tract income and child poverty\",\"description\":\"Four period maps of median household income in constant 2024 dollars and the share of children below the federal poverty threshold.\",\"temporalCoverage\":\"1999/2024\",\"isBasedOn\":[\"https://www.gwinnettcounty.com/static/departments/planning/Census/census_2000_selected_income_and_poverty_status_characteristics.pdf\",\"https://www2.census.gov/programs-surveys/acs/summary_file/\",\"https://api.censusreporter.org/1.0/data/show/acs2024_5yr?table_ids=B19013,B17001,B07010&geo_ids=05000US13135\",\"https://www2.census.gov/geo/tiger/\",\"https://data.bls.gov/timeseries/CUUR0000SA0\",\"https://services3.arcgis.com/jEYjQXUX2JTVoctH/ArcGIS/rest/services/High_School_Zone_22_23/FeatureServer/21\"],\"spatialCoverage\":\"Gwinnett County, Georgia\"}]}</script><style>*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:#faf9f5;color:#202d32;font:19px/1.65 Georgia,serif}header,main{max-width:790px;margin:auto;padding:0 21px}header{padding-top:22px;border-top:7px solid #1d5246}header b,nav,.src,figcaption,small,table,summary,label,button,.meta{font-family:Arial,sans-serif}.brand{color:#245749;letter-spacing:.04em}h1{font-size:clamp(39px,6vw,66px);line-height:1.02;letter-spacing:-.045em;margin:30px 0 15px}h2{margin:2em 0 .4em;font-size:clamp(28px,4vw,38px);line-height:1.13;letter-spacing:-.025em}.meta,small,.src{font-size:14px}.src{line-height:1.55;color:#394d48}.hero{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:5px;margin:19px 0}a{color:#215f50;text-underline-offset:3px}nav{border-block:1px solid #abb6ae;padding:14px 0;font-size:15px}figure{margin:24px 0 8px;background:white;border:1px solid #c5cfc8;padding:cla